/**
 * @packageDocumentation
 *
 * The journal engine's one effectful store: every directory walk, file read,
 * and file write behind the `journal` namespace (`journal.mjs`) lives here.
 * Reads and writes are not split into separate `read-journal-*`/
 * `write-journal-*` modules the way `heads.mjs`'s two independent functions
 * are (see `read-journal-heads.mjs`/`write-journal-heads.mjs`): the causal
 * admission index (events) and the legacy-projection backfill (the derived
 * artifact tiers) each make a *read* trigger a *write* -- admitting a
 * received witness is the read path's own backfill, not a side channel --
 * so a read/write module pair here would import each other, one hull file
 * pretending to be two. `src/lib/filesystem/index.mjs` sets the same
 * precedent: one module for a whole effect domain, no read/write split.
 *
 * Every pure law this store composes keeps living, and keeps its name, in
 * the hull module its callers already used before this split: content-
 * address and admission-index path arithmetic and the EAVT/event codec in
 * `events.mjs`; head-index path arithmetic in `heads.mjs`; the read-through
 * cache's pure law in `territory-cache.mjs`; the legacy sidecar path in
 * `legacy-codec.mjs`; packet path arithmetic and the atomic-term/datom-
 * reading laws in `index.mjs`. This module supplies only the effect those
 * laws are computed against or written through.
 */
